# Skill: Accessibility

Purpose:
  Ensure UI implementations meet WCAG 2.1 AA baseline and project
  accessibility requirements.

Owns: design/accessibility.sdd
ID: DESIGN-ACCESSIBILITY

Domain: design

Level: L3

Status: STABLE

Use:
  - Accessibility audits
  - A11y regression testing
  - Inclusive design validation

Input:
  - UI implementation
  - Accessibility requirements
  - WCAG target level

Output:
  - Accessibility violation list
  - Severity and compliance level
  - Remediation guidance

Baseline (WCAG 2.1 AA):
  - Perceivable: text alternatives, captions, adaptable content
  - Operable: keyboard accessible, enough time, seizures safe
  - Understandable: readable, predictable, input assistance
  - Robust: compatible with assistive technologies

Execute:
  1. Semantic HTML audit: headings, landmarks, labels
  2. Keyboard navigation: tab order, focus indicators, traps
  3. Screen reader: ARIA labels, live regions, alt text
  4. Color contrast: text/background >= 4.5:1 (3:1 for large text)
  5. Motion: respect prefers-reduced-motion
  6. Forms: labels, error messages, autocomplete
  7. Touch targets: minimum 44x44px

Severity:
  BLOCK: keyboard trap, missing alt on informative image, contrast < 3:1
  WARN: missing label, non-descriptive link text, focus indicator absent
  PASS: meets baseline

Validation:
  - No BLOCK violations in production
  - WARN violations tracked as technical debt

Avoid:
  - Treating accessibility as afterthought
  - Relying on color alone to convey information

State: +
